EXT. DRIVE-IN THEATER - NIGHT

A black-and-white monster movie flickers on the screen. Rows of empty cars. One pickup parked dead center.

SADIE QUILLEN (30s, trench coat) slides out of her sedan. Walks the aisle. Hands in pockets.

A STRANGER (40s, flat cap) sits on the pickup's tailgate. Eating popcorn.

SADIE
You're early.

STRANGER
You're slow.

Behind him, BIG TOMMY SERRANO (50s, enormous, suspenders) rises from the truck bed. Silent. Holding a tire iron.

SADIE
You brought a friend.

STRANGER
Insurance.

Sadie smiles. A click in the dark. From another car, a gun barrel. DETECTIVE LUCIA ORTEGA (40s, badge on a chain) steps into the screen's glow.

ORTEGA
Hands up. All of you.

Tommy swings. Sadie ducks. The Stranger hurls popcorn. Ortega fires into the sky. Everyone dives. The film's monster roars on the screen.

Sadie rolls under the pickup. Tommy drops the iron.

ORTEGA (CONT'D)
(to the Stranger)
Name.

STRANGER
Elias Brandt.

ORTEGA
Elias. Thank you.

ELIAS
(softly)
Wait. Wrong answer.

He grins. The truck's engine roars to life.
